 "_": [
  "FILM 8 -- The Night the Sea Comes Ashore (desh-east). 🧭 AAJ.",
  "",
  "THE PRIMITIVE IS `many`, and it is `troop` at a scale where hand-placing is not a thing a",
  "person does. A hundred thousand olive ridleys come ashore in a night and the film needs a",
  "beach 'cobbled with turtles as far as a torch could shine', so a hundred instances of one",
  "drawing have to read as a crowd rather than as wallpaper.",
  "",
  "`troop` puts n along a LINE. `many` fills an AREA with depth, and its failure modes are",
  "different and worse: a visible lattice, flat scale so the beach has no depth, and pile-ups",
  "that read as one broken shape. So placement is a jittered grid -- a lattice with a large",
  "random offset inside each cell -- which gives dense uneven spacing with no rejection loop;",
  "SIZE IS A FUNCTION OF THE ROW, so a turtle cannot be at the back and the size of one at the",
  "front; and it is seeded, so the render is byte-identical between runs.",
  "",
  "film.js then measures the count, that depth never inverts, that nearest-neighbour spacing",
  "has real variance (a lattice's is near zero), and that nobody is drawn through anybody.",
  "",
  "THE BADGE IS AAJ AND THAT CHANGES THINGS. This is a claim about a real coast, so nothing",
  "here is invented past the app's own text, the turtles are olive ridleys and not the",
  "Panchatantra tortoise, and there is no hero turtle in any shot. NO CALLOUTS: nobody in this",
  "film speaks, and a bubble over a wild animal would make a factual film into a cartoon.",
  "",
  "CAST COST: one new character, drawn from above so a crowd of it stays anonymous."
 ],
